-- ccc22-evidence.l4 -- sections 655 to 659 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46 (Part XX: evidence on trial: admissions; the valuable minerals presumption; statement of the accused; affidavits on ownership, value and identity information; theft and possession; expert testimony; proof of age; children's evidence). Part agent ccc22. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- How a result reads: JUST TRUE (the text's own words bring the case within the rule); JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words); NOTHING (not covered). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Tags in the comments: [M-a] a failed "if"/"where" or a flat negative counted as the text's no; [M-b] a prohibition or grant limited by its own wording counted as NOT the text's no (NOTHING);
-- [F:...] a fork line for NOTES.md (may-if, may-where, entitled, duty, unless). Section 2 terms and other parts' answers are INPUTS named for their section.

§ `Sections 655 to 657 -- Admissions; valuable minerals; statement of the accused`

-- src:13131 | 655 Where an accused is on trial for an indictable offence, he or his counsel may admit any fact alleged against him for the purpose of dispensing with proof thereof.
@ref s 655 (src:13131-13131)
GIVEN `the accused is on trial for an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the accused or their counsel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fact is alleged against the accused and the admission is for the purpose of dispensing with proof of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 655 the accused or their counsel may admit the fact` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the accused is on trial for an indictable offence` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an accused is on trial for an indictable offence, he or his counsel may admit any fact alleged against him" [F:may-where] [M-a]
        IF NOT (`the person is the accused or their counsel` AND `the fact is alleged against the accused and the admission is for the purpose of dispensing with proof of it`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "he or his counsel may admit any fact alleged against him for the purpose of dispensing with proof thereof"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:13133 | 656 In any proceeding in relation to theft or possession of a valuable mineral that is unrefined, partly refined, uncut or otherwise unprocessed by any person actively engaged in or on a mine, if it is established that the person possesses the valuable mineral, the person is presumed, in the absence of evidence raising a reasonable doubt to the contrary, to have stolen or unlawfully possessed the valuable mineral.
@ref s 656 (src:13133-13133)
GIVEN `the proceeding is in relation to theft or possession of a valuable mineral that is unrefined, partly refined, uncut or otherwise unprocessed by a person actively engaged in or on a mine` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is established that the person possesses the valuable mineral` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence raising a reasonable doubt to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 656 the person is presumed to have stolen or unlawfully possessed the valuable mineral` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the proceeding is in relation to theft or possession of a valuable mineral that is unrefined, partly refined, uncut or otherwise unprocessed by a person actively engaged in or on a mine` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In any proceeding in relation to theft or possession of a valuable mineral that is unrefined, partly refined, uncut or otherwise unprocessed by any person actively engaged in or on a mine"
        IF NOT `it is established that the person possesses the valuable mineral` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it is established that the person possesses the valuable mineral, the person is presumed" [M-a]
        IF `there is evidence raising a reasonable doubt to the contrary` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the absence of evidence raising a reasonable doubt to the contrary" [F:unless] [M-a]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:13135 | 657 A statement made by an accused under subsection 541(3) and purporting to be signed by the justice before whom it was made may be given in evidence against the accused at his or her trial without proof of the signature of the justice, unless it is proved that the justice by whom the statement purports to be signed did not sign it.
@ref s 657 (src:13135-13135)
GIVEN `the statement was made by an accused under subsection 541(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement purports to be signed by the justice before whom it was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved that the justice by whom the statement purports to be signed did not sign it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 657 the statement may be given in evidence against the accused without proof of the signature of the justice` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the statement was made by an accused under subsection 541(3)` AND `the statement purports to be signed by the justice before whom it was made`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A statement made by an accused under subsection 541(3) and purporting to be signed by the justice before whom it was made"
        IF `it is proved that the justice by whom the statement purports to be signed did not sign it` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless it is proved that the justice by whom the statement purports to be signed did not sign it" [F:unless] [M-a]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 657.1 -- Proof of ownership and value of property`

-- src:13137 | 657.1 (1) In any proceedings, an affidavit or a solemn declaration of a person who claims to be the lawful owner of, or the person lawfully entitled to possession of, property that was the subject-matter of the offence, or any other person who has specialized knowledge of the property or of that type of property, containing the statements referred to in subsection (2), shall be admissible in evidence and, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, is evidence of the statements contained in the affidavit or solemn declaration without proof of the signature of the person appearing to have signed the affidavit or solemn declaration.
@ref s 657.1(1) (src:13137-13137)
GIVEN `the person claims to be the lawful owner of, or the person lawfully entitled to possession of, property that was the subject-matter of the offence, or is any other person who has specialized knowledge of the property or of that type of property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit or solemn declaration contains the statements referred to in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 657.1(1) the affidavit or solemn declaration is admissible in evidence` MEANS
    IF `the person claims to be the lawful owner of, or the person lawfully entitled to possession of, property that was the subject-matter of the offence, or is any other person who has specialized knowledge of the property or of that type of property` AND `the affidavit or solemn declaration contains the statements referred to in subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an affidavit or a solemn declaration of a person who claims to be the lawful owner of, or the person lawfully entitled to possession of, property ... containing the statements referred to in subsection (2), shall be admissible in evidence"

-- src:13137 | 657.1 (1) In any proceedings, an affidavit or a solemn declaration of a person who claims to be the lawful owner of, or the person lawfully entitled to possession of, property that was the subject-matter of the offence, or any other person who has specialized knowledge of the property or of that type of property, containing the statements referred to in subsection (2), shall be admissible in evidence and, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, is evidence of the statements contained in the affidavit or solemn declaration without proof of the signature of the person appearing to have signed the affidavit or solemn declaration.
@ref s 657.1(1) (src:13137-13137)
GIVEN `the affidavit or solemn declaration is admissible under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 657.1(1) the affidavit or solemn declaration is evidence of the statements contained in it without proof of the signature` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the affidavit or solemn declaration is admissible under subsection (1)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an affidavit or a solemn declaration ... shall be admissible in evidence and ... is evidence of the statements"
        IF `there is evidence to the contrary` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the absence of evidence to the contrary, is evidence of the statements contained in the affidavit or solemn declaration" [F:unless] [M-a]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (2): a person shall state (a) lawful owner/entitled/specialised knowledge; (b) the value; (c) in the case of an owner or person entitled to possession, deprivation by fraudulent means or otherwise without lawful consent; (c.1) in a section 342 case, that the credit card had been revoked or cancelled, is a false document or was never issued; (d) the facts within personal knowledge relied on.
-- src:13139 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), a person shall state in an affidavit or a solemn declaration
-- src:13140 | (a) that the person is the lawful owner of, or is lawfully entitled to possession of, the property, or otherwise has specialized knowledge of the property or of property of the same type as that property;
-- src:13141 | (b) the value of the property;
-- src:13142 | (c) in the case of a person who is the lawful owner of or is lawfully entitled to possession of the property, that the person has been deprived of the property by fraudulent means or otherwise without the lawful consent of the person;
-- src:13143 | (c.1) in the case of proceedings in respect of an offence under section 342, that the credit card had been revoked or cancelled, is a false document within the meaning of section 321 or that no credit card that meets the exact description of that credit card was ever issued; and
-- src:13144 | (d) any facts within the personal knowledge of the person relied on to justify the statements referred to in paragraphs (a) to (c.1).
@ref s 657.1(2) (src:13139-13144)
GIVEN `the person states that the person is the lawful owner of, or is lawfully entitled to possession of, the property, or otherwise has specialized knowledge of the property or of property of the same type as that property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person states the value of the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the lawful owner of or is lawfully entitled to possession of the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person states that the person has been deprived of the property by fraudulent means or otherwise without the lawful consent of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are in respect of an offence under section 342` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person states that the credit card had been revoked or cancelled, is a false document within the meaning of section 321 or that no credit card that meets the exact description of that credit card was ever issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person states any facts within the personal knowledge of the person relied on to justify the statements referred to in paragraphs (a) to (c.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 657.1(2) the affidavit or solemn declaration states everything subsection (2) requires` MEANS
    IF `the person states that the person is the lawful owner of, or is lawfully entitled to possession of, the property, or otherwise has specialized knowledge of the property or of property of the same type as that property`
       AND `the person states the value of the property`
       AND ((NOT `the person is the lawful owner of or is lawfully entitled to possession of the property`) OR `the person states that the person has been deprived of the property by fraudulent means or otherwise without the lawful consent of the person`)
       AND ((NOT `the proceedings are in respect of an offence under section 342`) OR `the person states that the credit card had been revoked or cancelled, is a false document within the meaning of section 321 or that no credit card that meets the exact description of that credit card was ever issued`)
       AND `the person states any facts within the personal knowledge of the person relied on to justify the statements referred to in paragraphs (a) to (c.1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "For the purposes of subsection (1), a person shall state in an affidavit or a solemn declaration" the statements in paragraphs (a) to (d) (paragraph (c) only "in the case of a person who is the lawful owner of or is lawfully entitled to possession of the property", paragraph (c.1) only "in the case of proceedings in respect of an offence under section 342") [F:duty] [M-a]

-- src:13146 | (3) Unless the court orders otherwise, no affidavit or solemn declaration shall be received in evidence pursuant to subsection (1) unless the prosecutor has, before the trial or other proceeding, given to the accused a copy of the affidavit or solemn declaration and reasonable notice of intention to produce it in evidence.
@ref s 657.1(3) (src:13146-13146)
GIVEN `the court orders otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor has, before the trial or other proceeding, given to the accused a copy of the affidavit or solemn declaration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor has given the accused reasonable notice of intention to produce it in evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 657.1(3) the subsection bars receiving the affidavit or solemn declaration in evidence under subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `the court orders otherwise` OR (`the prosecutor has, before the trial or other proceeding, given to the accused a copy of the affidavit or solemn declaration` AND `the prosecutor has given the accused reasonable notice of intention to produce it in evidence`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless the court orders otherwise, no affidavit or solemn declaration shall be received in evidence pursuant to subsection (1) unless the prosecutor has, before the trial or other proceeding, given to the accused a copy of the affidavit or solemn declaration and reasonable notice of intention to produce it in evidence" (an exception is met) [F:unless] [M-a]
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:13148 | (4) Notwithstanding subsection (1), the court may require the person who appears to have signed an affidavit or solemn declaration referred to in that subsection to appear before it for examination or cross-examination in respect of the issue of proof of any of the statements contained in the affidavit or solemn declaration.
@ref s 657.1(4) (src:13148-13148)
GIVEN `the person appears to have signed an affidavit or solemn declaration referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 657.1(4) the court may require the person to appear for examination or cross-examination in respect of the issue of proof of any of the statements` MEANS
    IF `the person appears to have signed an affidavit or solemn declaration referred to in subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court may require the person who appears to have signed an affidavit or solemn declaration referred to in that subsection"

§ `Section 657.2 -- Theft and possession; accessory after the fact`

-- src:13150 | 657.2 (1) Where an accused is charged with possession of any property obtained by the commission of an offence, evidence of the conviction or discharge of another person of theft of the property is admissible against the accused, and in the absence of evidence to the contrary is proof that the property was stolen.
@ref s 657.2(1) (src:13150-13150)
GIVEN `the accused is charged with possession of property obtained by the commission of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence is of the conviction or discharge of another person of theft of the property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 657.2(1) the evidence of the conviction or discharge of another person of theft of the property is admissible against the accused` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the accused is charged with possession of property obtained by the commission of an offence` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an accused is charged with possession of any property obtained by the commission of an offence, evidence of the conviction or discharge of another person of theft of the property is admissible against the accused" [M-a]
        IF NOT `the evidence is of the conviction or discharge of another person of theft of the property` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "evidence of the conviction or discharge of another person of theft of the property"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:13150 | 657.2 (1) Where an accused is charged with possession of any property obtained by the commission of an offence, evidence of the conviction or discharge of another person of theft of the property is admissible against the accused, and in the absence of evidence to the contrary is proof that the property was stolen.
@ref s 657.2(1) (src:13150-13150)
GIVEN `the evidence is admissible against the accused under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 657.2(1) the evidence is proof that the property was stolen` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the evidence is admissible against the accused under subsection (1)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "evidence of the conviction or discharge of another person of theft of the property is admissible against the accused, and in the absence of evidence to the contrary is proof that the property was stolen"
        IF `there is evidence to the contrary` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the absence of evidence to the contrary is proof that the property was stolen" [F:unless] [M-a]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:13152 | (2) Where an accused is charged with being an accessory after the fact to the commission of an offence, evidence of the conviction or discharge of another person of the offence is admissible against the accused, and in the absence of evidence to the contrary is proof that the offence was committed.
@ref s 657.2(2) (src:13152-13152)
GIVEN `the accused is charged with being an accessory after the fact to the commission of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence is of the conviction or discharge of another person of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 657.2(2) the evidence of the conviction or discharge of another person of the offence is admissible against the accused` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the accused is charged with being an accessory after the fact to the commission of an offence` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an accused is charged with being an accessory after the fact to the commission of an offence, evidence of the conviction or discharge of another person of the offence is admissible against the accused" [M-a]
        IF NOT `the evidence is of the conviction or discharge of another person of the offence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "evidence of the conviction or discharge of another person of the offence"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:13152 | (2) Where an accused is charged with being an accessory after the fact to the commission of an offence, evidence of the conviction or discharge of another person of the offence is admissible against the accused, and in the absence of evidence to the contrary is proof that the offence was committed.
@ref s 657.2(2) (src:13152-13152)
GIVEN `the evidence is admissible against the accused under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 657.2(2) the evidence is proof that the offence was committed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the evidence is admissible against the accused under subsection (2)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "evidence of the conviction or discharge of another person of the offence is admissible against the accused, and in the absence of evidence to the contrary is proof that the offence was committed"
        IF `there is evidence to the contrary` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the absence of evidence to the contrary is proof that the offence was committed" [F:unless] [M-a]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 657.3 -- Expert testimony`

-- src:13154 | 657.3 (1) In any proceedings, the evidence of a person as an expert may be given by means of a report accompanied by the affidavit or solemn declaration of the person, setting out, in particular, the qualifications of the person as an expert if
-- src:13155 | (a) the court recognizes that person as an expert; and
-- src:13156 | (b) the party intending to produce the report in evidence has, before the proceeding, given to the other party a copy of the affidavit or solemn declaration and the report and reasonable notice of the intention to produce it in evidence.
@ref s 657.3(1) (src:13154-13156)
GIVEN `the evidence of the person as an expert is given by means of a report accompanied by the affidavit or solemn declaration of the person, setting out, in particular, the qualifications of the person as an expert` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court recognizes that person as an expert` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party intending to produce the report in evidence has, before the proceeding, given to the other party a copy of the affidavit or solemn declaration and the report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party has given the other party reasonable notice of the intention to produce it in evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 657.3(1) the evidence of the person as an expert may be given by means of a report accompanied by the affidavit or solemn declaration` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the evidence of the person as an expert is given by means of a report accompanied by the affidavit or solemn declaration of the person, setting out, in particular, the qualifications of the person as an expert` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the evidence of a person as an expert may be given by means of a report accompanied by the affidavit or solemn declaration of the person, setting out, in particular, the qualifications of the person as an expert"
        IF `the court recognizes that person as an expert` AND `the party intending to produce the report in evidence has, before the proceeding, given to the other party a copy of the affidavit or solemn declaration and the report` AND `the party has given the other party reasonable notice of the intention to produce it in evidence` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if (a) the court recognizes that person as an expert; and (b) the party intending to produce the report in evidence has, before the proceeding, given to the other party a copy of the affidavit or solemn declaration and the report and reasonable notice of the intention to produce it in evidence" [F:may-if]

-- src:13158 | (2) Notwithstanding subsection (1), the court may require the person who appears to have signed an affidavit or solemn declaration referred to in that subsection to appear before it for examination or cross-examination in respect of the issue of proof of any of the statements contained in the affidavit or solemn declaration or report.
@ref s 657.3(2) (src:13158-13158)
GIVEN `the person appears to have signed an affidavit or solemn declaration referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 657.3(2) the court may require the person to appear for examination or cross-examination in respect of the issue of proof of any of the statements` MEANS
    IF `the person appears to have signed an affidavit or solemn declaration referred to in subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court may require the person who appears to have signed an affidavit or solemn declaration referred to in that subsection"

-- (3)(a): the notice is due at least thirty days before the commencement of the trial, or within any other period fixed by the justice or judge. The fixed period, if any, is an input: the last day it allows.
-- src:13159 | Notice for expert testimony
-- src:13160 | (3) For the purpose of promoting the fair, orderly and efficient presentation of the testimony of witnesses,
-- src:13161 | (a) a party who intends to call a person as an expert witness shall, at least thirty days before the commencement of the trial or within any other period fixed by the justice or judge, give notice to the other party or parties of his or her intention to do so, accompanied by
-- src:13162 | (i) the name of the proposed witness,
-- src:13163 | (ii) a description of the area of expertise of the proposed witness that is sufficient to permit the other parties to inform themselves about that area of expertise, and
-- src:13164 | (iii) a statement of the qualifications of the proposed witness as an expert;
@ref s 657.3(3)(a) (src:13159-13164)
GIVEN `the day the trial commences` IS A DATE
      `the last day allowed by any other period fixed by the justice or judge` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 657.3(3)(a) the last day for the notice of the expert witness` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day allowed by any other period fixed by the justice or judge`
    WHEN JUST fixed THEN fixed
    WHEN NOTHING THEN Date (Day `the day the trial commences` MINUS 30)

-- src:13159 | Notice for expert testimony
-- src:13160 | (3) For the purpose of promoting the fair, orderly and efficient presentation of the testimony of witnesses,
-- src:13161 | (a) a party who intends to call a person as an expert witness shall, at least thirty days before the commencement of the trial or within any other period fixed by the justice or judge, give notice to the other party or parties of his or her intention to do so, accompanied by
-- src:13162 | (i) the name of the proposed witness,
-- src:13163 | (ii) a description of the area of expertise of the proposed witness that is sufficient to permit the other parties to inform themselves about that area of expertise, and
-- src:13164 | (iii) a statement of the qualifications of the proposed witness as an expert;
@ref s 657.3(3)(a) (src:13159-13164)
GIVEN `the party intends to call a person as an expert witness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the trial commences` IS A DATE
      `the last day allowed by any other period fixed by the justice or judge` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the notice was given` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the notice is accompanied by the name of the proposed witness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is accompanied by a description of the area of expertise of the proposed witness that is sufficient to permit the other parties to inform themselves about that area of expertise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is accompanied by a statement of the qualifications of the proposed witness as an expert` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 657.3(3)(a) the party has given the notice the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF NOT `the party intends to call a person as an expert witness`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a party who intends to call a person as an expert witness shall"
    ELSE
        (CONSIDER `the day the notice was given`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN
            (IF `the day asked about` GREATER THAN `s 657.3(3)(a) the last day for the notice of the expert witness` `the day the trial commences` `the last day allowed by any other period fixed by the justice or judge`
             THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall, at least thirty days before the commencement of the trial or within any other period fixed by the justice or judge, give notice" (the last day has passed and no notice was given) [F:duty] [M-a]
             ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the last day for the notice has not passed, so no duty is yet unmet
         WHEN JUST given THEN
            (IF given AT MOST `s 657.3(3)(a) the last day for the notice of the expert witness` `the day the trial commences` `the last day allowed by any other period fixed by the justice or judge` AND `the notice is accompanied by the name of the proposed witness` AND `the notice is accompanied by a description of the area of expertise of the proposed witness that is sufficient to permit the other parties to inform themselves about that area of expertise` AND `the notice is accompanied by a statement of the qualifications of the proposed witness as an expert`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall, at least thirty days before the commencement of the trial or within any other period fixed by the justice or judge, give notice to the other party or parties of his or her intention to do so, accompanied by (i) the name of the proposed witness, (ii) a description of the area of expertise ..., and (iii) a statement of the qualifications of the proposed witness as an expert" (late, or not so accompanied) [F:duty] [M-a]

-- src:13165 | (b) in addition to complying with paragraph (a), a prosecutor who intends to call a person as an expert witness shall, within a reasonable period before trial, provide to the other party or parties
-- src:13166 | (i) a copy of the report, if any, prepared by the proposed witness for the case, and
-- src:13167 | (ii) if no report is prepared, a summary of the opinion anticipated to be given by the proposed witness and the grounds on which it is based; and
@ref s 657.3(3)(b) (src:13165-13167)
GIVEN `the person is a prosecutor who intends to call a person as an expert witness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor provided the material within a reasonable period before trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a report was prepared by the proposed witness for the case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor provided a copy of the report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor provided a summary of the opinion anticipated to be given by the proposed witness and the grounds on which it is based` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 657.3(3)(b) the prosecutor has provided the material the paragraph requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is a prosecutor who intends to call a person as an expert witness` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a prosecutor who intends to call a person as an expert witness shall"
        IF NOT `the prosecutor provided the material within a reasonable period before trial` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall, within a reasonable period before trial, provide to the other party or parties" [F:duty] [M-a]
        IF `a report was prepared by the proposed witness for the case` THEN
            (IF `the prosecutor provided a copy of the report` THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(i) a copy of the report, if any, prepared by the proposed witness for the case" [F:duty] [M-a]
        OTHERWISE
            (IF `the prosecutor provided a summary of the opinion anticipated to be given by the proposed witness and the grounds on which it is based` THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(ii) if no report is prepared, a summary of the opinion anticipated to be given by the proposed witness and the grounds on which it is based" [F:duty] [M-a]

-- (3)(c): the accused, or counsel, shall provide the same material not later than the close of the case for the prosecution (calendar rule, then the regulative twin).
-- src:13168 | (c) in addition to complying with paragraph (a), an accused, or his or her counsel, who intends to call a person as an expert witness shall, not later than the close of the case for the prosecution, provide to the other party or parties the material referred to in paragraph (b).
@ref s 657.3(3)(c) (src:13168-13168)
GIVEN `the accused or their counsel intends to call a person as an expert witness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the material was provided` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the case for the prosecution closes` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 657.3(3)(c) the accused or their counsel has provided the material not later than the close of the case for the prosecution` MEANS
    IF NOT `the accused or their counsel intends to call a person as an expert witness`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an accused, or his or her counsel, who intends to call a person as an expert witness shall"
    ELSE
        (CONSIDER `the day the material was provided`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN
            (IF `the day asked about` GREATER THAN `the day the case for the prosecution closes`
             THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall, not later than the close of the case for the prosecution, provide to the other party or parties the material" (the case for the prosecution has closed and nothing was provided) [F:duty] [M-a]
             ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the case for the prosecution has not closed, so no duty is yet unmet
         WHEN JUST provided THEN
            (IF provided AT MOST `the day the case for the prosecution closes`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not later than the close of the case for the prosecution" (provided late) [F:duty] [M-a]

-- src:13168 | (c) in addition to complying with paragraph (a), an accused, or his or her counsel, who intends to call a person as an expert witness shall, not later than the close of the case for the prosecution, provide to the other party or parties the material referred to in paragraph (b).
@ref s 657.3(3)(c) (src:13168-13168)
DECLARE `s 657.3(3)(c) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 657.3(3)(c) provide the material referred to in paragraph (b) to the other party or parties`

@ref s 657.3(3)(c) (src:13168-13168)
GIVEN `the time of the close of the case for the prosecution` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 657.3(3)(c) action`
`s 657.3(3)(c) the accused must provide the material before the close of the case for the prosecution` MEANS
    PARTY `the accused`
    MUST `s 657.3(3)(c) provide the material referred to in paragraph (b) to the other party or parties`
    WITHIN `the time of the close of the case for the prosecution`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the accused, who intends to call a person as an expert witness, did not provide the material before the close of the case for the prosecution"

-- src:13170 | (4) If a party calls a person as an expert witness without complying with subsection (3), the court shall, at the request of any other party,
-- src:13171 | (a) grant an adjournment of the proceedings to the party who requests it to allow him or her to prepare for cross-examination of the expert witness;
@ref s 657.3(4)(a) (src:13170-13171)
GIVEN `the party called a person as an expert witness without complying with subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another party requests an adjournment to prepare for cross-examination of the expert witness` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 657.3(4)(a) the court must grant an adjournment to the party who requests it` MEANS
    IF `the party called a person as an expert witness without complying with subsection (3)` AND `another party requests an adjournment to prepare for cross-examination of the expert witness`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a party calls a person as an expert witness without complying with subsection (3), the court shall, at the request of any other party, (a) grant an adjournment of the proceedings to the party who requests it" [F:duty] [M-a]

-- src:13170 | (4) If a party calls a person as an expert witness without complying with subsection (3), the court shall, at the request of any other party,
-- src:13171 | (a) grant an adjournment of the proceedings to the party who requests it to allow him or her to prepare for cross-examination of the expert witness;
-- src:13172 | (b) order the party who called the expert witness to provide that other party and any other party with the material referred to in paragraph (3)(b); and
@ref s 657.3(4)(b) (src:13170-13172)
GIVEN `the party called a person as an expert witness without complying with subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another party requests the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 657.3(4)(b) the court must order the party who called the expert witness to provide the material referred to in paragraph (3)(b)` MEANS
    IF `the party called a person as an expert witness without complying with subsection (3)` AND `another party requests the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a party calls a person as an expert witness without complying with subsection (3), the court shall, at the request of any other party, ... (b) order the party who called the expert witness to provide that other party and any other party with the material referred to in paragraph (3)(b)" [F:duty] [M-a]

-- src:13170 | (4) If a party calls a person as an expert witness without complying with subsection (3), the court shall, at the request of any other party,
-- src:13171 | (a) grant an adjournment of the proceedings to the party who requests it to allow him or her to prepare for cross-examination of the expert witness;
-- src:13172 | (b) order the party who called the expert witness to provide that other party and any other party with the material referred to in paragraph (3)(b); and
-- src:13173 | (c) order the calling or recalling of any witness for the purpose of giving testimony on matters related to those raised in the expert witness’s testimony, unless the court considers it inappropriate to do so.
@ref s 657.3(4)(c) (src:13170-13173)
GIVEN `the party called a person as an expert witness without complying with subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another party requests the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court considers it inappropriate to order the calling or recalling of the witness` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 657.3(4)(c) the court must order the calling or recalling of any witness for the purpose of giving testimony on matters related to those raised in the expert witness’s testimony` MEANS
    IF `the party called a person as an expert witness without complying with subsection (3)` AND `another party requests the order` AND (NOT `the court considers it inappropriate to order the calling or recalling of the witness`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the court shall, at the request of any other party, ... (c) order the calling or recalling of any witness ..., unless the court considers it inappropriate to do so" (no request, or the court considers it inappropriate) [F:duty] [F:unless] [M-a]

DECLARE `s 657.3(5) the order` IS ONE OF
    `s 657.3(5)(a) adjourn the proceedings`
    `s 657.3(5)(b) order that further particulars be given of the evidence of the proposed witness`
    `s 657.3(5)(c) order the calling or recalling of any witness for the purpose of giving testimony on matters related to those raised in the expert witness’s testimony`
    `s 657.3(5) some other order`

-- src:13175 | (5) If, in the opinion of the court, a party who has received the notice and material referred to in subsection (3) has not been able to prepare for the evidence of the proposed witness, the court may do one or more of the following:
-- src:13176 | (a) adjourn the proceedings;
-- src:13177 | (b) order that further particulars be given of the evidence of the proposed witness; and
-- src:13178 | (c) order the calling or recalling of any witness for the purpose of giving testimony on matters related to those raised in the expert witness’s testimony.
@ref s 657.3(5) (src:13175-13178)
GIVEN `a party has received the notice and material referred to in subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the court, the party has not been able to prepare for the evidence of the proposed witness` IS A BOOLEAN
      order IS A `s 657.3(5) the order`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 657.3(5) the court may make the order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF order EQUALS `s 657.3(5) some other order` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the court may do one or more of the following: (a) adjourn the proceedings; (b) order that further particulars be given ...; and (c) order the calling or recalling of any witness"
        IF NOT (`a party has received the notice and material referred to in subsection (3)` AND `in the opinion of the court, the party has not been able to prepare for the evidence of the proposed witness`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If, in the opinion of the court, a party who has received the notice and material referred to in subsection (3) has not been able to prepare for the evidence of the proposed witness, the court may" [F:may-if]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:13180 | (6) If the proposed witness does not testify, the prosecutor may not produce material provided to him or her under paragraph (3)(c) in evidence without the consent of the accused.
@ref s 657.3(6) (src:13180-13180)
GIVEN `the proposed witness does not testify` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the material was provided to the prosecutor under paragraph (3)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 657.3(6) the subsection bars the prosecutor from producing the material in evidence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the proposed witness does not testify` AND `the material was provided to the prosecutor under paragraph (3)(c)`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the proposed witness does not testify, the prosecutor may not produce material provided to him or her under paragraph (3)(c) in evidence"
        IF `the accused consents` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without the consent of the accused" [M-b]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:13182 | (7) Unless otherwise ordered by a court, information disclosed under this section in relation to a proceeding may only be used for the purpose of that proceeding.
@ref s 657.3(7) (src:13182-13182)
GIVEN `the purpose is the purpose of that proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a court has ordered otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 657.3(7) the subsection bars using the information disclosed under the section for a purpose other than that proceeding` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a court has ordered otherwise` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless otherwise ordered by a court" [F:unless] [M-a]
        IF `the purpose is the purpose of that proceeding` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may only be used for the purpose of that proceeding" (a use for that proceeding is what the subsection allows; it bars no other)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 657.4 -- Proof of absence of consent: identity information`

-- (5): identity information has the meaning section 402.1 gives it: the answer is the section 402.1 input (another part), passed through.
-- src:13196 | (5) In this section, identity information has the same meaning as in section 402.1.
@ref s 657.4(5) (src:13196-13196)
GIVEN `s 402.1 the information is identity information` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 657.4(5) the information is identity information` MEANS `s 402.1 the information is identity information`   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "identity information has the same meaning as in section 402.1"

-- src:13184 | 657.4 (1) In any proceedings in relation to an offence under section 402.2 or 403, an affidavit or a solemn declaration of a person whose identity information was used or was obtained or possessed with intent to be used to commit an indictable offence that includes fraud, deceit or falsehood as an element of the offence, containing the statements referred to in subsection (2), is admissible in evidence and, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, is evidence of the statements contained in the affidavit or solemn declaration without proof of the signature of the person appearing to have signed the affidavit or solemn declaration.
@ref s 657.4(1) (src:13184-13184)
GIVEN `the proceedings are in relation to an offence under section 402.2 or 403` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information of the person was used or was obtained or possessed with intent to be used to commit an indictable offence that includes fraud, deceit or falsehood as an element of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 657.4(5) for the information` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit or solemn declaration contains the statements referred to in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 657.4(1) the affidavit or solemn declaration is admissible in evidence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer of s 657.4(5) for the information`
    WHEN JUST isId THEN
        (IF `the proceedings are in relation to an offence under section 402.2 or 403` AND isId AND `the information of the person was used or was obtained or possessed with intent to be used to commit an indictable offence that includes fraud, deceit or falsehood as an element of the offence` AND `the affidavit or solemn declaration contains the statements referred to in subsection (2)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In any proceedings in relation to an offence under section 402.2 or 403, an affidavit or a solemn declaration of a person whose identity information was used or was obtained or possessed with intent to be used to commit an indictable offence that includes fraud, deceit or falsehood as an element of the offence, containing the statements referred to in subsection (2), is admissible in evidence"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the information is identity information is for section 402.1

-- src:13184 | 657.4 (1) In any proceedings in relation to an offence under section 402.2 or 403, an affidavit or a solemn declaration of a person whose identity information was used or was obtained or possessed with intent to be used to commit an indictable offence that includes fraud, deceit or falsehood as an element of the offence, containing the statements referred to in subsection (2), is admissible in evidence and, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, is evidence of the statements contained in the affidavit or solemn declaration without proof of the signature of the person appearing to have signed the affidavit or solemn declaration.
@ref s 657.4(1) (src:13184-13184)
GIVEN `the affidavit or solemn declaration is admissible under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 657.4(1) the affidavit or solemn declaration is evidence of the statements contained in it without proof of the signature` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the affidavit or solemn declaration is admissible under subsection (1)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an affidavit or a solemn declaration of a person whose identity information was used ... is admissible in evidence and ... is evidence of the statements"
        IF `there is evidence to the contrary` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the absence of evidence to the contrary, is evidence of the statements contained in the affidavit or solemn declaration" [F:unless] [M-a]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:13186 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), a person shall state in an affidavit or a solemn declaration
-- src:13187 | (a) that the person is the person whose identity information was used or intended to be used to commit the offence;
-- src:13188 | (b) the nature of the identity information that was used or intended to be used to commit the offence;
-- src:13189 | (c) that the person did not consent to the use of their identity information by the accused; and
-- src:13190 | (d) any facts within the personal knowledge of the person relied on to justify the statements referred to in paragraphs (b) and (c).
@ref s 657.4(2) (src:13186-13190)
GIVEN `the person states that the person is the person whose identity information was used or intended to be used to commit the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person states the nature of the identity information that was used or intended to be used to commit the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person states that the person did not consent to the use of their identity information by the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person states any facts within the personal knowledge of the person relied on to justify the statements referred to in paragraphs (b) and (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 657.4(2) the affidavit or solemn declaration states everything subsection (2) requires` MEANS
    IF `the person states that the person is the person whose identity information was used or intended to be used to commit the offence` AND `the person states the nature of the identity information that was used or intended to be used to commit the offence` AND `the person states that the person did not consent to the use of their identity information by the accused` AND `the person states any facts within the personal knowledge of the person relied on to justify the statements referred to in paragraphs (b) and (c)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "For the purposes of subsection (1), a person shall state in an affidavit or a solemn declaration" the four statements in paragraphs (a) to (d) [F:duty] [M-a]

-- src:13192 | (3) Unless the court orders otherwise, no affidavit or solemn declaration is to be received in evidence under subsection (1) unless the prosecutor has, before the trial or other proceeding, given to the accused a copy of the affidavit or solemn declaration and reasonable notice of their intention to produce it in evidence.
@ref s 657.4(3) (src:13192-13192)
GIVEN `the court orders otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor has, before the trial or other proceeding, given to the accused a copy of the affidavit or solemn declaration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor has given the accused reasonable notice of their intention to produce it in evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 657.4(3) the subsection bars receiving the affidavit or solemn declaration in evidence under subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `the court orders otherwise` OR (`the prosecutor has, before the trial or other proceeding, given to the accused a copy of the affidavit or solemn declaration` AND `the prosecutor has given the accused reasonable notice of their intention to produce it in evidence`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless the court orders otherwise, no affidavit or solemn declaration is to be received in evidence under subsection (1) unless the prosecutor has, before the trial or other proceeding, given to the accused a copy of the affidavit or solemn declaration and reasonable notice of their intention to produce it in evidence" (an exception is met) [F:unless] [M-a]
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:13194 | (4) Despite subsection (1), the court may require the person who appears to have signed an affidavit or solemn declaration referred to in that subsection to appear before it for examination or cross-examination in respect of the issue of proof of any of the statements contained in the affidavit or solemn declaration.
@ref s 657.4(4) (src:13194-13194)
GIVEN `the person appears to have signed an affidavit or solemn declaration referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 657.4(4) the court may require the person to appear for examination or cross-examination in respect of the issue of proof of any of the statements` MEANS
    IF `the person appears to have signed an affidavit or solemn declaration referred to in subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court may require the person who appears to have signed an affidavit or solemn declaration referred to in that subsection"

§ `Section 658 -- Children and young persons: proof of age`

-- src:13200 | 658 (1) In any proceedings to which this Act applies, the testimony of a person as to the date of his or her birth is admissible as evidence of that date.
@ref s 658(1) (src:13200-13200)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings to which this Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the testimony is the testimony of a person as to the date of their own birth` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 658(1) the testimony of a person as to the date of their birth is admissible as evidence of that date` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are proceedings to which this Act applies` AND `the testimony is the testimony of a person as to the date of their own birth`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In any proceedings to which this Act applies, the testimony of a person as to the date of his or her birth is admissible as evidence of that date"

-- src:13202 | (2) In any proceedings to which this Act applies, the testimony of a parent as to the age of a person of whom he or she is a parent is admissible as evidence of the age of that person.
@ref s 658(2) (src:13202-13202)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings to which this Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the testimony is the testimony of a parent as to the age of a person of whom they are a parent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 658(2) the testimony of a parent as to the age of a person of whom they are a parent is admissible as evidence of the age of that person` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are proceedings to which this Act applies` AND `the testimony is the testimony of a parent as to the age of a person of whom they are a parent`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In any proceedings to which this Act applies, the testimony of a parent as to the age of a person of whom he or she is a parent is admissible as evidence of the age of that person"

-- src:13203 | Proof of age
-- src:13204 | (3) In any proceedings to which this Act applies,
-- src:13205 | (a) a birth or baptismal certificate or a copy of such a certificate purporting to be certified under the hand of the person in whose custody the certificate is held is evidence of the age of that person; and
@ref s 658(3)(a) (src:13203-13205)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings to which this Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is a birth or baptismal certificate or a copy of such a certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document purports to be certified under the hand of the person in whose custody the certificate is held` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 658(3)(a) the certificate or copy is evidence of the age of that person` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are proceedings to which this Act applies` AND `the document is a birth or baptismal certificate or a copy of such a certificate` AND `the document purports to be certified under the hand of the person in whose custody the certificate is held`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a birth or baptismal certificate or a copy of such a certificate purporting to be certified under the hand of the person in whose custody the certificate is held is evidence of the age of that person"

-- src:13206 | (b) an entry or record of an incorporated society or its officers who have had the control or care of a child or young person at or about the time the child or young person was brought to Canada is evidence of the age of the child or young person if the entry or record was made before the time when the offence is alleged to have been committed.
@ref s 658(3)(b) (src:13206-13206)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings to which this Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is an entry or record of an incorporated society or its officers who have had the control or care of a child or young person at or about the time the child or young person was brought to Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entry or record was made before the time when the offence is alleged to have been committed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 658(3)(b) the entry or record is evidence of the age of the child or young person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the proceedings are proceedings to which this Act applies` AND `the document is an entry or record of an incorporated society or its officers who have had the control or care of a child or young person at or about the time the child or young person was brought to Canada`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an entry or record of an incorporated society or its officers who have had the control or care of a child or young person at or about the time the child or young person was brought to Canada"
        IF `the entry or record was made before the time when the offence is alleged to have been committed` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is evidence of the age of the child or young person if the entry or record was made before the time when the offence is alleged to have been committed" [M-a]

-- src:13208 | (4) In the absence of any certificate, copy, entry or record mentioned in subsection (3), or in corroboration of any such certificate, copy, entry or record, a jury, judge, justice or provincial court judge, as the case may be, may receive and act on any other information relating to age that they consider reliable.
@ref s 658(4) (src:13208-13208)
GIVEN `there is no certificate, copy, entry or record mentioned in subsection (3), or the information is in corroboration of any such certificate, copy, entry or record` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the jury, judge, justice or provincial court judge, as the case may be, considers the information reliable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 658(4) the jury, judge, justice or provincial court judge may receive and act on the other information relating to age` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the jury, judge, justice or provincial court judge, as the case may be, considers the information reliable` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any other information relating to age that they consider reliable"
        IF NOT `there is no certificate, copy, entry or record mentioned in subsection (3), or the information is in corroboration of any such certificate, copy, entry or record` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the absence of any certificate, copy, entry or record mentioned in subsection (3), or in corroboration of any such certificate, copy, entry or record" [F:may-where] [M-a]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:13210 | (5) In the absence of other evidence, or by way of corroboration of other evidence, a jury, judge, justice or provincial court judge, as the case may be, may infer the age of a child or young person from his or her appearance.
@ref s 658(5) (src:13210-13210)
GIVEN `there is no other evidence, or the inference is by way of corroboration of other evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a child or young person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 658(5) the jury, judge, justice or provincial court judge may infer the age of the child or young person from their appearance` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is a child or young person` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may infer the age of a child or young person from his or her appearance"
        IF NOT `there is no other evidence, or the inference is by way of corroboration of other evidence` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the absence of other evidence, or by way of corroboration of other evidence" [F:may-where] [M-a]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 659 -- Children's evidence`

-- src:13214 | 659 Any requirement whereby it is mandatory for a court to give the jury a warning about convicting an accused on the evidence of a child is abrogated.
@ref s 659 (src:13214-13214)
GIVEN `the requirement is a requirement whereby it is mandatory for a court to give the jury a warning about convicting an accused on the evidence of a child` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 659 the requirement is abrogated` MEANS
    IF `the requirement is a requirement whereby it is mandatory for a court to give the jury a warning about convicting an accused on the evidence of a child`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any requirement whereby it is mandatory for a court to give the jury a warning about convicting an accused on the evidence of a child is abrogated"
